      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the CL, based on review observation, it has:\n\n* `system/stack/include/l2cap_interface.h` that defines the main L2CAP interface\n* `system/stack/include/l2cap_api.h` that defines the Impl subclass that will be used for the actual L2CAP implementation\n* `system/stack/l2cap/l2cap_api.cc` that defines the content of the Impl class which redirects the function call to the next layer in l2c_api.h\n* `system/stack/l2cap/internal/l2c_api.h` that defines the C style L2CAP API\n* `system/stack/l2cap/l2c_api.cc` that defines the content of the C L2CAP API, where the actual implementation is\n\nThen there are two mocks of l2cap_interface.h\n* `system/test/mock/mock_stack_l2cap_interface.h`\n* `system/stack/test/l2cap_interface_mock.h`\n\nI think it can be simplified by removing some layers like this:\n\n* `system/stack/include/l2cap_interface.h` that defines the main L2CAP interface\n* `system/stack/include/l2cap_impl.h` that defines the Impl subclass that will be used for the actual L2CAP implementation (renamed from l2cap_api.h as api vs interface is a bit confusing)\n* `system/stack/l2cap/l2cap_impl.cc` that defines the content of the Impl class which directly defines the implementation, copy content from system/stack/l2cap/l2c_api.cc to here\n* `system/stack/l2cap/internal/l2c_api.h` delete\n* `system/stack/l2cap/l2c_api.cc` delete\n\nFor mocks, we can have a single definition shared with all tests\n* `system/stack/l2cap/include/l2cap_mock.h` defines the common mock interface\n* `system/stack/l2cap/l2cap_mock.cc` defines the common mock implementation to be shared with all tests\n\nLastly, it would be helpful to include content like above in the commit message so that reviewers can understand what architecture CL author is trying to achieve.\n\nCould you check if the CL can be simplified like suggested above?",
      "revId": "24d8e7b88316fe7d7328b7841feb7d309c1781a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
